### Summary

It would be great to have the capability to use CSS or Markdown to enhance the appearance of buttons generated by st.page_link(). 

### Why?

This would allow for customization of attributes such as background color, hover color, size, and more.

### How?

Example 1:

`st.page_link(
        "./pages/Home.py", 
        label="Home", 
        background_color="#007BFF", 
        hover_color="#0056b3", 
        text_color="white", 
        font_size="16px", 
        padding="10px 20px", 
        border_radius="4px"
    )`




Example 2:


```
button_style = """
  <style>
  .custom-button {
      background-color: #007BFF;
      color: white;
      border: none;
      border-radius: 4px;
      padding: 10px 20px;
      text-align: center;
      text-decoration: none;
      display: inline-block;
      font-size: 16px;
      margin: 4px 2px;
      cursor: pointer;
      transition-duration: 0.4s;
  }
.custom-button:hover {
    background-color: #0056b3;
    color: white;
}
</style>
"""

home_button = f'''
{button_style}
<a href="./pages/Home.py" target="_self">
    <button class="custom-button">Home</button>
</a>
'''

st.page_link("./pages/Home.,py", label=st.markdown(home_button, unsafe_allow_html=True))




